{"id": "DfBaXycoJ4x", "title": "Video by therishikatha", "description": "Why couldn’t BHIMA, the strongest of the Pandavas, lift an old monkey’s tail? 🐒 Because that “old monkey” was HANUMAN, his own elder brother! 🙏\n\nThis story is in the Mahabharata (Vana Parva). In the forest, a golden lotus blew in on the wind and Draupadi wanted more, so Bhima charged up the Gandhamadana mountain to find them. A sleepy monkey lay across his path in a banana grove.\n\n“I’m too sick to get up. Just jump over me,” said the monkey. Bhima refused: God lives in every creature, so he would not step over him. “Just move my tail aside, then.” Bhima grabbed it with one hand… then both. It didn’t move one inch.\n\nBhima bowed and asked who he was: “I am Hanuman.” Both were sons of Vayu, the wind god. Hanuman showed him the giant form in which he leapt the ocean, as tall as the Vindhya mountains, then shrank back and hugged his little brother. He promised to roar from Arjuna’s flag in the great war. 🚩\n\n📚 Stories like this, made for kids, are in our Rishi Katha picture books. Books 1–3: set of 3 for ₹500 at rishikatha.com (link in bio).\n\n💬 Did you know Bhima and Hanuman were brothers? Comment JAI HANUMAN 🙏\n🔁 Share it with someone who loves Mahabharata stories, and save it for your kids’ bedtime.\n\n#hanuman #bhima #mahabharata #jaihanuman #bajrangbali pandavas hindumythology indianmythology sanatandharma hanumanji mythologystories kidsstories bedtimestories rishikatha storytime", "channel": "therishikatha", "uploader_id": "22569163881", "uploader": "Rishi Katha", "timestamp": 1793156324, "like_count": 1527, "comment_count": 30, "http_headers": {"Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-1108916781549310a", "ext": "m4a", "tbr": 70.554, "asr": 44100, "format_note": "DASH audio", "container": "m4a_dash", "vcodec": "none", "acodec": "mp4a.40.5", "url": "https://instagram.fblr2-3.fna.fbcdn.net/o1/v/t2/f2/m78/AQPxKbqkjYQEum8KVclI4eUpwKcM_GL-jCr5yQVkOYTZ_HEW4hJ